        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಅನುಸರಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅನುಸರಿಸು — anusarisu — \"to comply with; to go by\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಎಲ್ಲಾ ಚಾಲಕರು ಸಿಗ್ನಲ್ ಅನುಸರಿಸಬೇಕು. ellā cālakaru signal anusarisabēku. All drivers must go by the signals."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಅನುಸರಿಸಿದೆ, anusariside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಿಯಮ ಅನುಸರಿಸು (anusarisu), to follow a rule; ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸು is to follow behind someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅನುಸರಿಸು (anusarisu) is built from Sanskrit anusaraṇa, \"going after\", the noun of anusarati, \"runs after, follows\" (CDIAL 338), with the verb ending -isu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
