          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಾಲಿಸು — pālisu — \"to obey; to keep (a rule)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾವು ಸಂಚಾರ ನಿಯಮಗಳನ್ನು ಪಾಲಿಸಿದೆವು. nāvu sañcāra niyamagaḷannu pālisidevu. We kept to the traffic rules."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಪಾಲಿಸಿದೆ, pāliside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also to look after or rear; ನಿಯಮ ಪಾಲಿಸು (pālisu) is the usual pair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಾಲಿಸು (pālisu) is built from Sanskrit pālayati, \"guards, protects\" (CDIAL 8129), with the Kannada verb ending -isu: to keep a rule is to guard it."
            }
          ]
        },
